summary: Test packaged IPA in qemu VMs on a KVM-capable guest
description: |
    The jobs are nested-qemu presets: each environment is a set of qemu VMs
    started on the guest, not podman containers. The guest therefore needs
    KVM: the request carries hardware.virtualization.is-supported (added
    by `freeipa-env queue run --runner testing-farm` when a job is a
    nested-qemu preset). tests/freeipa-env/qemu-prep.sh fetches the cloud
    images the presets name. The IPA comes from the preset's own vm.copr and
    vm.guest_packages, so the request's compose only picks the guest OS the
    VMs run on, not the release under test.
discover:
    how: fmf
    test: "^/tmt/tests/"
prepare:
    how: install
    package: [qemu-system-x86-core, qemu-img, xorriso, rsync, openssh-clients, python3-pyyaml, curl]
execute:
    how: tmt
